infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title On-demand vs continuous profiling
  desc Pay nothing until capture — but risk losing the evidence; or pay 2-5% always — and have the profile pre-saved
  compares
    - label On-demand: capture during the incident
      children
        - label Zero overhead between captures
          desc Cost only while perf record runs — nothing the rest of the time
        - label Needs you present, issue live
          desc At 2:14 AM, SSH in, reproduce under load, capture, parse — under pressure
        - label Intermittent issues lose the evidence
          desc Incidents that self-resolve are gone before you can capture them
    - label Continuous: always-on, pre-saved
      children
        - label 2-5% CPU, always sampling
          desc Agent on every host samples 100 Hz, ships compressed every 10-15s
        - label Incident profile already saved
          desc When an SLO burns, the flame graph for those minutes is in the backend
        - label ~50-200 MB/day per service
          desc Standing ~1.5-6 GB/month buys retroactive flame graphs for any moment
theme
  palette #f59e0b #14b8a6
